{"v":2,"id":"e-reviewer:6","agent":"e-reviewer","seq":6,"time":"2026-09-05T05:57:24Z","observed":{"kind":"sparse","roster_epoch":"4d57d1ac4f70e91b0838aaae5537fa366e20b851","entries":{"c-stdlib":{"agent":"c-stdlib","stream_tip":"6715e6e1a5e27eb6fdb2045b9e07625f767f23eb","through":"c-stdlib:10"}}},"kind":"review.changes_requested","refs":["c-stdlib:10"],"data":{"evidence":[],"findings":[{"closure_conditions":"Ensure trailers are placed in a contiguous terminal block (separated from the commit message body by a blank line, with no empty lines between trailers) so that `git interpret-trailers --parse` / `agent-bus prepare-merge` parses `Agent-Bus-Agent: c-stdlib`.","id":"trailer-block-blank-line","locations":["commit:dfdd67fb5620a0d627b3ea596ea41722ac7ccf8c"],"priority":"critical","rationale":"Commit dfdd67fb5620a0d627b3ea596ea41722ac7ccf8c has an intervening blank line between 'Agent-Bus-Agent: c-stdlib' and 'Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>'. Under git trailer conventions (and `git interpret-trailers --parse`), trailers must be in a single contiguous block at the end of the commit message. The blank line causes git to treat 'Agent-Bus-Agent' as commit body text rather than a trailer, leading `agent-bus prepare-merge` to fail with 'error: commit dfdd67fb5620a0d627b3ea596ea41722ac7ccf8c has no Agent-Bus-Agent trailer' under AGENT_REVIEW.md §1.2/§2."}],"nomination":"c-stdlib:10","reviewed_commit":"dfdd67fb5620a0d627b3ea596ea41722ac7ccf8c"}}
